<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaoundé</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yaoundé is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, set on hills in the centre-south of the country. It began as a German military and research station founded in 1889, became the capital of French-ruled Cameroon in the 1920s and has been the capital of independent Cameroon since 1960. It is the country's second-largest city after the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douala">Douala</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaounde.jpg" alt="Yaoundé" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Eavebe assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yaound%C3%A9_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
